      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does a gas safety certificate cost in Formby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A CP12 gas safety certificate costs £75 for the first gas appliance, with additional appliances at £10 each. A Formby property with a boiler and gas hob comes to £90 total, one visit, one certificate. A combined gas safety certificate and annual boiler service costs £150. Portfolio rates from £70 per property for two or more properties. No call-out fee.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">SELLING</span>&nbsp; Should I get a gas safety certificate before selling my Formby house?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes, and increasingly you need to. Formby buyers at higher price points are requesting gas safety documentation as part of their pre-exchange due diligence. A valid CP12 removes this as a potential late-stage objection. A CP12 inspection from £75 is one of the simplest and most cost-effective steps you can take before listing. We can often attend within 24 to 48 hours and email the certificate the same day for your solicitor.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">BUYING</span>&nbsp; Can I request an independent gas safety inspection before completing on a Formby property?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We carry out independent pre-completion CP12 inspections for Formby buyers. We inspect the boiler, gas cooker and hob and provide a written report on each one. This is separate from and more detailed than a homebuyer's survey. Any faults found are documented in writing and can be used to renegotiate the purchase price or request remedial work from the vendor before completion. The full inspection costs £80 for the boiler, plus £10 per additional appliance.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">MULTIPLE</span>&nbsp; Do you cover multiple gas appliances in one visit?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Many Formby properties have a boiler, a gas hob and sometimes a gas fire. We cover boilers, gas cookers and hobs in one visit. Each extra cooker or hob is £10, agreed before we start. One certificate, emailed the same day. We do not inspect gas fires. If you no longer need it, we can disconnect and cap it safely, so it no longer has to be on the certificate. If you want to keep using it, it must be checked by an engineer registered for gas fires.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are you Gas Safe registered for Formby CP12 certificates?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Liverpool Emergency Plumber is Gas Safe registered. Verify at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. All CP12 inspections in Formby are carried out by Gas Safe registered. All gas work is done by a Gas Safe registered plumber.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">LANDLORDS</span>&nbsp; I rent out a Formby property. What does my CP12 need to cover?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>The CP12 must cover every gas appliance supplied by you as the landlord, boiler, gas hob, gas fire, gas cooker. Anything gas-connected that was in the property when the tenant moved in is your responsibility. We cover the boiler, gas cooker and hob in one visit on one certificate. A gas fire must be checked by an engineer registered for gas fires, or we can disconnect and cap it safely. Annual reminder included so your certificate never lapses.</p></div></details>
